<section class="text">
  <h1>Hi, I’m Ale Muñoz, Product Design Engineer</h1>
  <p>
    I've spent two decades <strong
      >building tools for the people who build things</strong
    >.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://sketch.com">Design tools</a>. <a href="https://zenrows.com"
      >Development tools</a
    >. <a href="https://qatium.com">Engineering Tools</a>. <a
      href="https://bebanjo.com">Productivity tools</a
    >. I've built tools for myself, for my teams, and for the public. I've built
    communities, and I've built products. I've built things that have been used
    by millions of people, and things that have been used by just a handful of
    people.
  </p>
  <p>
    I've worked at the intersection of design and technology for as long as I
    can remember. I'm comfortable with all steps of the product process and can
    do 0 to 1 product development, but my true passion is designing things and
    bringing them to life.
  </p>
  <p>I also love orange, but can use other colors.</p>
  <p>
    You can read more about <a href="/how-i-work">how I work</a>, or check some
    of my recent projects below.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm currently open to senior product design roles. Get in touch by <a
      href="mailto:bomberstudios@gmail.com">email</a
    >, on <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/bomberstudios.com">Bluesky</a> or <a
      href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/bomberstudios/">LinkedIn</a
    >.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="text" id="projects">
  <h2>Projects</h2>
  <p>
    As a designer with many years of experience, I use both my skills and my <em
      >intuition</em
    > to create simple solutions to complex problems. I enjoy my craft and <a
      href="https://ale.today/polish-polish-polish"
      >love to work on the details</a
    >, but I always try to reach the sweet spot between “this is perfect” and
    “we need this yesterday”.
  </p>
  <p>
    These are some recent projects that (I believe) illustrate these points.
  </p>
</section>

